SUMMARY:Heartland Marimba Festival – FREE
DESCRIPTION:Make the Ware Center part of your Lancaster First Friday route!
  7 pm • Lobby Uncover the fascinating history and science behind the mar
 imba with members of Heartland Marimba. This special presentation explores
  how the instrument produces its distinctive sound\, traces its journey fr
 om Africa through Central America to the classical music stage\, and revea
 ls the surprising Pennsylvania connections behind its history. Discover ho
 w U.S. companies and performers helped introduce the marimba to classical 
 music\, and hear the untold stories of the musicians who shaped the instru
 ment’s legacy. Among them is Clair Musser\, widely regarded as the “go
 dfather” of the classical marimba\, who was born in Manheim\, Pennsylvan
 ia. The story continues in Lancaster\, where Reg Kehoe performed across th
 e country for nearly 20 years with the Marimba Queens\, a popular all-fema
 le marimba ensemble based in Lancaster from the 1930s through the 1950s. W
 hether you are a longtime marimba enthusiast or simply curious about this 
 remarkable percussion instrument\, join Heartland Marimba for an engaging 
 look at marimba history\, music\, acoustics\, and its unique Pennsylvania 
 roots. Admission: FREE and open to the public! Accessibility: There will b
 e a pre-show touch tour for blind and low-vision patrons. Please get in to
 uch with Barry Kornhauser to learn more.\n\nPrice: Not supplied by this so
 urce\; check event details\n\nSchedule listed: Fri\, Nov 06\, 2026 07:00 P
